winch plan: show the changes and change nothing

Examples:
  # show the changes of the pipeline site
  winch plan site
  # use the inventory production
  winch plan site --inventory production
  # plan with a value for one variable
  winch plan site --set vars.nginx_port=8080
  # plan two stages on the web hosts without web3
  winch plan site --hosts 'web & !web3' --stages nginx,site
  # exit with code 2 when apply would change something
  winch plan site --exit-code

Usage:
  winch plan [<pipeline>] [flags]

Plan shows the changes that winch apply would make, and the plan hash.
It changes nothing.

Leave out the pipeline name when the steps are at the top of
winch.yaml.

A host pattern is a group or a host, with "," for union, "&" for
intersection, and "!" for exclusion. Each stage runs on the hosts in
both its hosts and --hosts. The stages of --stages run in pipeline
order.

A --set value parses as YAML.

With a terminal, ssh can ask questions, and winch connects to the
hosts one at a time. Without one, or with --batch, ssh asks nothing,
and winch connects to them in parallel.

With --exit-code, plan exits with code 2 when the plan has changes,
unknown steps, pending handlers, a pending then, or a pending gate or
assert.

Flags:
  --inventory <name>          inventory for the run
                              default: inventory in winch.yaml
  --hosts <pattern>           only these hosts
                              default: all
  --stages <names>            only these stages, such as mail,monit
                              default: all
  --user [<host>=]<name>      SSH login user, for all hosts or one;
                              repeatable
                              default: from the inventory
  --set vars.<name>=<value>   variable value; repeatable
  --batch                     no questions from ssh
  --exit-code                 exit code 2 for a plan with changes
  --json                      JSON events on stdout

See: winch doc workflow, winch doc pipeline, winch doc inventory
